eration  when even the united states last line of  defense the shd  had no idea maybe the black tusk was  given intel on his work  and it was them who first initiated  contact  like i said there would have to be a  number of pieces that came together in  order for this to work  and we really haven't been given  anything that would point in this  direction  but at the same time we haven't been  given anything to prove otherwise  so technically it's still a perfectly  valid theory  the hunters are black tusk  this would have to be the most popular  theory out there i don't really have to  explain this one so much it makes  complete sense after all we do actively  see the hunter working with the black  tusk in the manhunt  so they're obviously connected in some  way they would have also been the  perfect soldier type for hindering the  division's movement  in the beginning while still keeping the  btsu identity hidden  they could be a special unit of the  black tusk  but the question is are they black tusk  or are they simply working with them  this could explain what barton meant  earlier on before the invasion  when he told his boss that he already  had a team in mind and that they are the  baddest of the bad  ruthless cutthroats or something along  those lines  also the black tusks at one point after  revealing themselves  were given an order to back off from  taking down the division agents  if the hunters were black tusk they too  would have received the same order  which would explain why the hunters  later on in the division 2 were in a  more docile state in comparison to the  ones we met earlier on  we were the ones hunting them however  they seem somewhat distance from the  btsu  there seems to be far more to the story  than simply being a part of the btsu  like why have we not seen them earlier  in some of the more vital missions that  the division has managed to put a stop  to  sure it could be because they are more  suited to urban execution-style combat  but that wasn't exactly what we were  seeing from the hunter during the  manhunt  and why only one hunter the way barden  interacts with the hunter certainly  gives more of a feel that they're more  of a third party a hired gun  or a borrowed operative and then there  is natalia's knowledge  and questioning around the asset this  leads me to believe that there are more  to do with the next theory  the hunters are russian 100  the second most popular and probably the  longest surviving theory on the hunters  out there  the reason it's so strongly supported  today is because of the introduction of  a new name  natalia sokolova this surname is among  the 10 most common russian surnames  and although there is a small amount of  variation in the name it's quite likely  that she is in some way related to the  circle of concern  brand set or more specifically the  circle of corporation  now apparently this is common knowledge  although i certainly had no idea  but in russia it's often the case that  females of a family would have a slight  change to the surname  some of you would clearly be able to  explain this better than i and this  probably isn't the video to be talking  about it  but this has something to do with the  russian nouns having a gender associated  with them  and with feminine nouns they often end  with an ah or  sound i found it interesting  but i digress if natalya is in fact  related to the sokolov company  this would certainly explain the power  she has over barden schaefer  it's likely this large international  company has considerable financial  backing  and is among or perhaps the main  corporation behind the employment of the  black tusk  the hunters could be a unit of the  sokolov corporation  or dare i say it russian special forces  another somewhat obvious piece that has  always supported this theory  is the writings of the man himself tom  clancy  in his books it was relatively common to  find the antagonists to be russian  time and time again he will talk about  the highly trained and specialized  russian agents  sent to destabilize the us government  often they wouldn't be heard talking  instead communicating with bizarre  noises in an attempt to hide any  indication of their origin  sounds familiar right  this would also talk to the advanced  nature of the black tusk technology and  weapons  however there are a couple of points  enough people are brought up  that it's worth talking about for  example if natalia is part of the large  russian corporation  and is from russia where is the accent  to be honest it isn't too hard to  believe that she has learnt to hide the  accent  i mean this has been done countless  times over the years  plus look at actors things can be picked  up over time  and she could have been trained in this  since she was young for all we know  the hunter tattoos i talked about in an  earlier video these are very obviously  us military tattoos  so if they're a russian why would they  have them this could just be another way  of misleading and hiding their identity  or as i've said before they could simply  be a reused asset by the design team  but what about barden schaefer he is a  true patriot  and believes what he is doing is best  for the country  formerly in the military would he really  think that a russian-based corporation  would be the best thing for the united  states  well maybe he doesn't know the way  natalia talks to him  is quite vague he's perhaps in a  need-to-know situation  and this could also explain why she  talks to him with an american accent  again i still question why only one  hunter was sent in  surely they would have seen other  hunters have been taken down  but when you think about it the manhunt  was called concealed agenda  and we really weren't given much of an  idea of what baden was doing  maybe the hunter really was just being  used as a distraction along with the  rogue agents  to keep the division busy while barton  was doing whatever he was doing 